  "id": "fig-83",
  "mode": "hybrid",
  "description": "Two identical tuning forks on separate wooden resonance boxes with their openings facing each other; a small hammer is poised near one arm of the right fork. Inspect apparatus setup for sound resonance without displaying the result or the later clip experiment.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/10p/figures/fig-83.png",
      "sha256": "cec42cfeb8c8444a04e5556508b213cf47267bfef5c36d4a20c8caaf14ac0f1c"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "language": "en",
        "lesson": "phy10-c1-s5-n44",
        "text": "# 44. Sound Resonance\n\nSounding objects can vibrate freely.\nAn external periodic force can drive them.\nIf the force's frequency is near their natural frequency, resonance can greatly boost the response.\n\nTwo identical tuning forks demonstrate **sound resonance**.\nSet them a short distance apart on wooden resonance boxes.\nLet the box openings face each other (Figure 83).\n\nTap one arm of one fork with a small hammer.\nThe other fork soon begins to sound as well.\nSound waves from the first apply a periodic force to it.\n\nTheir matching natural frequencies allow a large response.\nThe response depends on the frequency difference.\nOutside the receiving fork's narrow resonance band, it is much weaker.\n\nAttach a light metal clip to either identical fork.\nThis shifts its natural frequency and can detune the pair.\nWith enough detuning, the response may become inaudible.\n\nFigure 83\n\nTuning forks have little damping, so their resonance curve is sharp.\nThis is the behavior discussed in Section 14.\n"
      },
      {
        "language": "zh",
        "lesson": "phy10-c1-s5-n44",
        "text": "# 44. 声的共鸣\n\n发声物体可以做自由振动。\n在周期性外力作用下，它也可以做受迫振动。\n外力频率接近物体的固有频率时，受迫振动可以显著增强，这就是共振。\n\n两只相同的音叉可以用来演示**声的共振**。\n把它们放在相隔不远的木制共鸣箱上。\n让两个木箱的开口彼此相对（图83）。\n\n用小锤轻敲一只音叉的一个臂。\n不久，另一只音叉也开始发声。\n第一只音叉发出的声波，对另一只施加周期性的力。\n\n两只音叉的固有频率相同，所以另一只可以产生较大的振动响应。\n若两只音叉的固有频率不同，响应强弱取决于频率相差多少。\n外力频率落在接收音叉的狭窄共振频带之外时，响应会弱得多。\n\n在原来相同的任一音叉上固定一个轻金属夹。\n金属夹会改变这只音叉的固有频率，使两只音叉可能失谐。\n失谐足够大时，响应会减弱，也可能听不到声音。\n\n图83\n\n音叉的振动阻尼较小，所以共振曲线比较尖锐。\n这与第14节的讨论一致。\n"
      }
    ],
